,title,link,text,language,family
0,Awad Bing language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Awad_Bing_language,"Awad Bing, or Biliau, is an Austronesian language spoken by about 1,100 people in seven villages near Astrolabe Bay, Madang Province, Papua New Guinea. Almost all speakers also use Tok Pisin as a second language.",Awad Bing,Austronesian
1,Awad Bing language,https://grokipedia.com/page/awad_bing_language,"Awad Bing is an Austronesian language spoken by approximately 1,450 people (as of 2000) in six main villages—Suit, Galeg, Malangai, Yamai, Teterai, and Biliau—and scattered hamlets along the Rai Coast of Madang Province, Papua New Guinea, from 8 to 20 kilometers west of Saidor.",Awad Bing,Austronesian
2,Awad Bing / Biliau - Max Planck Society,https://lingweb.eva.mpg.de/channumerals/Awad-Bing.htm,"Awad Bing, or Biliau, is an Austronesian language spoken by about 1,100 people in seven villages near Astrolabe Bay, Madang Province, Papua New Guinea. Almost all speakers also use Tok Pisin as a second language.",Awad Bing,Austronesian
3,(PDF) The Phonology and Orthography of Awad Bing - Academia.edu,https://www.academia.edu/6916780/The_Phonology_and_Orthography_of_Awad_Bing,"Feb 3, 2025 · This paper explores the phonological and orthographic characteristics of Awad Bing, focusing on consonant co-occurrences. It analyzes how consonants interact within words and the implications for phonetic representation.",Awad Bing,Austronesian
