5,The Phonology and Orthography of Awad Bing | SIL Global,https://www.sil.org/resources/archives/57104,This paper has been written to provide an organised report of the work done so far in the analysis of the phonology of the Awad Bing language and of the recommendations and problems with regard to developing a feasible orthography.,Awad Bing,Austronesian
6,Awad Bing language explained,https://everything.explained.today/Biliau/,"Awad Bing, or Biliau, is an Austronesian language spoken by about 1,100 people in seven villages near Astrolabe Bay, Madang Province, Papua New Guinea. Almost all speakers also use Tok Pisin as a second language.",Awad Bing,Austronesian
7,"Awad Bing: Biliau language. Evangelism tools, church planting ...",https://globalrecordings.net/en/language/615,"Audio recordings available in Awad Bing: Biliau These recordings are designed for evangelism and basic Bible teaching to bring the gospel message to people who are not literate or are from oral cultures, particularly unreached people groups.",Awad Bing,Austronesian
8,Awad Bing | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/bcu/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..6wiFjmR96ylaOhyum4BRMF7QhaxCfFWlFD625lALCG8,Awad Bing is a stable indigenous language of Papua New Guinea. It belongs to the Austronesian language family. The language is used as a first language by all in the ethnic community.,Awad Bing,Austronesian
9,Austronesian Music - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLnOSH5j1sQh9pFS_rqvm3r2JtCD8AGOa-,"Play all. Austronesian Music. by steven white. • Playlist • 90 videos • 8,743 views. Austronesian culture includes more than 1200 ethnic groups, across South Asia, Southeast Asia, Taiwan, the Philippines, parts of China, as well as the Pacific as far afield as the Maori in New Zealand.",Awad Bing,Austronesian
